Job Description
• Responsible for all global and regional consultant databases, and third-party database providers;
• Working closely with the consultant relationship management teams to understand the role of each consultant, their strategic importance and the competitive landscape;
• Ensuring accurate, high quality and consistent updating of quantitative and qualitative information in multiple consultant databases (eVestment, Mercer GIMD, Camradata, WTW, etc.);
• Adding new products to the consultant databases in close collaboration with Investment Management teams and various other subject matter experts within the firm;
• Actively participating and representing the CSLM team in the regular consultant coordination calls;
• Collaborating with colleagues regarding the further development of data tools and data quality improvement;
• Production of analysis using database analytical tools (competitive analyses, product views, trending product themes, regions, etc.);
• Completing consultant driven questionnaires and ad-hoc requests when required;
• Supporting the team in projects.
Requirements
• University degree, ideally in finance or a quantitative field;
• 3-5 years relevant experience within the asset management industry, ideally in a similar or adjacent role;
• Excellent Microsoft Office skills, in Word and Excel, including complex spreadsheet development;
• Fluent command of English, additional language skills especially German would be considered beneficial;
• Efficient and precise working style with high attention to detail in a deadline-oriented environment;
• Service-oriented team player with the ability to build good relationships with internal content contributors;
• International mindset, self-motivated and ability to work independently.
What to expect
• New employees at LGT Capital Partners begin with numerous introductions from the heads of all the departments at the firm. You will receive training and orientation on our businesses and gain technical and practical knowledge.
You will make an impact by:
• Working with the Business Development and Investment Management teams while gaining in-depth exposure to liquid market asset classes;
• Working with global and local consultants, and third-party database providers to provide quantitative and qualitative analysis, conduct market research;
• Collaborative working culture with a flat, non-hierarchical structure that will enable you to work directly with portfolio managers and partners;
• Ongoing learning and training opportunities to help you acquire new skills or deepen existing expertise;
• Locations you can work in: Pfaeffikon (near Zurich) Switzerland or London.
Contact Information
If you are interested in becoming an integral part of a successful alternative investment management team in an international, multicultural working environment we will be pleased to get to know you soon.
For further information please contact us.
